<%#
  The button that says this page is worth passing on.

  Every one of these pages already draws itself a picture for the preview, and until
  now nothing on the page said so: the card only existed for whoever pasted the link.
  What is shared is the page's own canonical, which is what the crawler is told too.
%>
<%# The face says "Share" on every page, because a button that reads "Share this
    player" beside a back link is what stopped the two fitting on one row of a
    phone. What is being shared is still said, just not in ink: a screen reader
    hears it and the share sheet is titled with it. %>
<button type="button" data-controller="share"
        data-share-url-value="<%= local_assigns.fetch(:url, meta_url) %>"
        data-share-title-value="<%= local_assigns.fetch(:title, meta_title) %>"
        <%= tag.attributes("aria-label": local_assigns[:aria_label]) if local_assigns[:aria_label] %>
        data-action="share#share"
        class="inline-flex shrink-0 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg border border-zinc-200 px-3 py-1.5 text-sm font-medium text-zinc-700 hover:border-zinc-400 hover:text-zinc-950">
  <svg class="size-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
    <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"
          d="M7.217 10.907a2.25 2.25 0 100 2.186m0-2.186c.18.324.283.696.283 1.093s-.103.77-.283 1.093m0-2.186l9.566-5.314m-9.566 7.5l9.566 5.314m0 0a2.25 2.25 0 103.935 2.186 2.25 2.25 0 00-3.935-2.186zm0-12.814a2.25 2.25 0 103.933-2.185 2.25 2.25 0 00-3.933 2.185z"/>
  </svg>
  <span data-share-target="label"><%= local_assigns.fetch(:label, "Share") %></span>
</button>
